			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Well thank you for recognizing the "pain" that it is.
<br />

<br />
If you would ask your members to get one person to make a list of interested toons, and then have one person send a tell to our officers (preferably an officer to verify they're recruits)  will smooth things allot for us.
<br />

<br />
Last raid, i know i got mega tells, and so did rave.  Sad part was that some of these unguilded people are saying they are recruits to CE, or wudan or sod  and when we finally get a hold of an officer from that guild to verify, find out they've never heard of that toon!  Nearly 50% of the unguilded people hanging around were NOT recruits from any of the guilds on the rotations.
<br />

<br />
Other funny one I see is someone will hang around the raid, just put up LFG tag and hope they'll get an invite, and not say a word.  hehe
<br />

<br />
The bad part is, that it all takes time to check on these people, and that's time that's taken away from the raid. 
<br />

<br />
If it continues to be bad, Rave has said she'll close our raids to non tagged people period.  Since many other guilds don't flag their recruits, this would be a real problem.  So please have one person send a tell,   with a list of all who wish to come on a raid, and able to confirm the recruit status of all, will make the raid get started much smoother.
<br />

<br />
Thanks
<br />

<br />
